#: ../../Operation/Coagulant_Automation.rst:69
msgid "Coagulant Dose for Dissolved Organic Matter"
msgstr "dosis de coagulante para materia orgánica disuelta"

#: ../../Operation/Coagulant_Automation.rst:71
msgid ""
"The next improvement in this simple model is to add a correction factor for "
"dissolved organic matter. The dissolved organic matter effectively "
"inactivates some of the coagulant. The dissolved organic matter is measured "
"as absorbance at 254 nm. The amount of coagulant that is tied up with "
"dissolved organic matter is"
msgstr ""
"La siguiente mejora en este modelo sencillo es añadir un factor de "
"corrección para la materia orgánica disuelta. La materia orgánica disuelta "
"inactiva efectivamente parte del coagulante. La materia orgánica disuelta se"
" mide como absorbancia a 254 nm. La cantidad de coagulante que se atará a la"
" materia orgánica disuelta es"

#: ../../Operation/Coagulant_Automation.rst:73
msgid "C_{coag_{DOM}}  = A_{254nm} K_{DOM}"
msgstr "C_{coag_{DOM}} = A_{254nm} K_{DOM}"

#: ../../Operation/Coagulant_Automation.rst:78
msgid ""
"The dissolved organic matter simply reduces the amount of coagulant that is "
"available to make the inorganic particles sticky. The required coagulant "
"dose can be obtained by adding :math:`C_{coag_{DOM}}` to Equation "
":eq:`Ccoagkpf`."
msgstr ""
"La materia orgánica disuelta simplemente reduce la cantidad de coagulante "
"disponible para que las partículas inorgánicas sean pegajosas. La dosis de "
"coagulante necesaria puede obtenerse añadiendo :math:`C_{coag_{DOM}}` a la "
"Ecuación :eq:`Ccoagkpf`."

#: ../../Operation/Coagulant_Automation.rst:80
msgid ""
"C_{coag} =  k_{pf} C_{P_0} \\left(C_{P}^{-2/3}-C_{P_0}^{-2/3}\\right) + "
"C_{coag_{DOM}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Operation/Coagulant_Automation.rst:85
#, python-format
msgid ""
"One method to estimate :math:`K_{DOM}` is based on the experimental results "
"obtained by Yingda Du (see :numref:`figure_floc_model_HA` `by Yingda Du, et "
"al., 2019 <https://www.liebertpub.com/doi/abs/10.1089/ees.2018.0405>`_). "
"Those results suggest that approximately 1 mg/L of aluminum is required to "
"tie up 12 mg/L of humic acid.  The humic acid concentration was based on the"
" dry weight and humic acid is approximately 48% carbon. Thus 6 mg of humic "
"acid as carbon require 1 mg/L of aluminum. The absorbance at 254 nm was "
"measured by `Rodrigues. et al., 2008 "
"<https://core.ac.uk/reader/55618110?utm_source=linkout>`_  to be 0.055(humic"
" acid as carbon in mg/L). Thus :math:`0.33A_{254nm}` is expected to consume "
"1 mg/L of aluminum where :math:`A_{254nm}` is the UV 254 absorbance in a 1 "
"cm sample cell. The remaining required conversion is from the concentration "
"of aluminum to the coagulant dose as measured at the water treatment plant."
msgstr ""
"Un método para estimar :math:`K_{DOM}` se basa en los resultados "
"experimentales obtenidos por Yingda Du (véase :numref:`figure_floc_model_HA`"
" `de Yingda Du, et al., 2019 "
"<https://www.liebertpub.com/doi/abs/10.1089/ees.2018.0405>`_). Estos "
"resultados sugieren que se requiere aproximadamente 1 mg/L de aluminio para "
"asegurar 12 mg/L de ácido húmico. La concentración de ácido húmico se basó "
"en el peso seco y el ácido húmico es aproximadamente un 48% de carbono. Así,"
" 6 mg de ácido húmico como carbono requieren 1 mg/L de aluminio. La "
"absorbancia a 254 nm fue medida por `Rodrigues. et al., 2008 "
"<https://core.ac.uk/reader/55618110?utm_source=linkout>`_ como 0,055 (ácido "
"húmico como carbono en mg/L). Por tanto, se espera que :math:`0.33A_{254nm}`"
" consuma 1 mg/L de aluminio, donde :math:`A_{254nm}` es la absorbancia UV "
"254 en una celda de muestra de 1 cm. La conversión restante requerida es de "
"la concentración de aluminio a la dosis de coagulante medida en la planta "
"tratamiento de agua ."

#: ../../Operation/Coagulant_Automation.rst:87
msgid ""
"Equation :eq:`Ccoagtotal` can be rewritten with subscripts that indicate "
"when and where the samples are taken for the application of automatic "
"coagulant dosing. The tube settler turbidity in the future, "
":math:`C_{TS_{flocculated_{t + \\theta}}}` is the target turbidity of "
"flocculated water after passing through a tube settler that we are trying to"
" obtain."
msgstr ""
"La ecuación :eq:`Ccoagtotal` puede reescribirse con subíndices que indiquen "
"cuándo y dónde se toman las muestras para la aplicación de la dosificación "
"automática de coagulantes. La turbidez del sedimentador tubular en el futuro"
" :math:`C_{TS_{flocculated_{t + \\theta}}}` es la turbidez objetivo del agua"
" floculada tras pasar por un sedimentador tubular que intentamos obtener."

#: ../../Operation/Coagulant_Automation.rst:89
msgid ""
"C_{coag_{t}} = k_{pf} C_{raw_{t}} \\left(C_{TS_{flocculated_{t + "
"\\theta}}}^{-2/3}-C_{raw_{t}}^{-2/3}\\right) + C_{coag_{DOM_{t}}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Operation/Coagulant_Automation.rst:94
msgid ""
"Equation :eq:`CcoagplantFlocculatedTS` reveals that there is an important "
"time lag due to the hydraulic retention time between the coagulant injection"
" and the clarified water sample. This time lag will require that the dosing "
"algorithm include data from the recent history to account for this time "
"offset."
msgstr ""
"La ecuación :eq:`CcoagplantFlocculatedTS` revela que existe un retardo "
"temporal importante debido al tiempo de retención hidráulica entre la "
"inyección de coagulante y la muestra agua clarificada . Este retardo "
"requerirá que el algoritmo de dosificación incluya datos del historial "
"reciente para tener en cuenta este desplazamiento temporal."

#: ../../Operation/Coagulant_Automation.rst:97
msgid "Simple Corrector Method"
msgstr "Método Simple Corrector"

#: ../../Operation/Coagulant_Automation.rst:99
msgid ""
"An estimate for the coagulant demand of the DOM is obtained by solving "
"Equation :eq:`CcoagplantFlocculatedTS` for :math:`C_{coag_{DOM_{t}}}` and "
"shifting the time to one hydraulic residence time earlier."
msgstr ""
"Se obtiene una estimación de la demanda de coagulante del DOM resolviendo la"
" Ecuación :eq:`CcoagplantFlocculatedTS` para :math:`C_{coag_{DOM_{t}}}` y "
"desplazando el tiempo a un tiempo de residencia hidráulico antes."

#: ../../Operation/Coagulant_Automation.rst:101
msgid ""
"C_{coag_{DOM_{t-\\theta}}} = C_{coag_{t-\\theta}} - k_{pf} "
"C_{raw_{t-\\theta}} "
"\\left(C_{TS_{flocculated_{t}}}^{-2/3}-C_{raw_{t-\\theta}}^{-2/3}\\right)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Operation/Coagulant_Automation.rst:106
msgid ""
"Given the estimate of the DOM coagulant demand a hydraulic residence time "
"earlier we can obtain an estimate of the current required coagulant dose. We"
" will use Equation :eq:`CcoagplantFlocculatedTS` and the assumption that the"
" coagulant DOM demand doesn't change significantly in one hydraulic "
"residence time. The :math:`C_{TS_{flocculated_{t + \\theta}}` is the target "
"tube settler turbidity."
msgstr ""
"Dada la estimación de la demanda de coagulante del DOM y un tiempo de "
"residencia hidráulica anterior, podemos obtener una estimación de la "
"corriente requerida dosis de coagulante. Utilizaremos la Ecuación "
":eq:`CcoagplantFlocculatedTS` y la suposición de que la demanda del DOM del "
"coagulante no cambia significativamente en un tiempo de residencia "
"hidráulico. La :math:`C_{TS_{flocculated_{t + \\theta}}` es la turbidez del "
"sedimentador del tubo objetivo."

#: ../../Operation/Coagulant_Automation.rst:108
msgid ""
"C_{coag_{t}} =  k_{pf} C_{raw_{t}} \\left(C_{TS_{flocculated_{t + "
"\\theta}}}^{-2/3}-C_{raw_{t}}^{-2/3}\\right) + C_{coag_{DOM_{t-\\theta}}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Operation/Coagulant_Automation.rst:113
msgid ""
"The coagulant dosing system must include guardrails to ensure that the "
"coagulant dose is within a reasonable range. The potential failures include:"
msgstr ""
"El sistema de dosificación de coagulantes debe incluir barreras de seguridad"
" para asegurar que el dosis de coagulante esté dentro de un rango razonable."
" Los posibles fallos incluyen:"

#: ../../Operation/Coagulant_Automation.rst:115
msgid ""
"incorrect reading from a turbidimeter due to an air bubble, a dirty sample "
"cell, or during routine maintenance"
msgstr ""
"lectura incorrecta de un turbidímetro debido a una burbuja de aire, una "
"celda de muestra sucia o durante el mantenimiento rutinario"

#: ../../Operation/Coagulant_Automation.rst:116
msgid ""
"settled water turbidity that is very low because the plant is starting up "
"after an extended shutdown"
msgstr ""
"agua sedimentada turbidez que es muy baja porque la planta arranca tras un "
"apagado prolongado"

#: ../../Operation/Coagulant_Automation.rst:118
msgid ""
"Another potential failure mode would occur if the raw water turbidity is "
"lower than the target clarified turbidity. This would result in a coagulant "
"dose that could be too low to achieve effective filtration."
msgstr ""
"Otro posible modo de fallo ocurriría si la turbidez agua cruda es menor que "
"la turbidez clarificada objetivo. Esto resultaría en un dosis de coagulante "
"que podría ser demasiado bajo para lograr una filtración efectiva."

#: ../../Operation/Coagulant_Automation.rst:120
msgid ""
"To reduce the likelihood of a treatment failure the estimated DOM coagulant "
"demand can be compared with a reasonable range and if it is out of that "
"range the estimated DOM coagulant demand can be forced back into the "
"reasonable range. To prevent an excessively low coagulant dose the DOM "
"coagulant demand can be limited to positive values. If it is known that the "
"DOM coagulant demand is always exceeds a larger value, that larger value can"
" be used as a lower limit. The upper limit can be set based on observation "
"of the raw water quality."
msgstr ""
"Para reducir la probabilidad de un fallo del tratamiento, la demanda "
"estimada de coagulante DOM puede compararse con un rango razonable y, si "
"está fuera de ese rango, la demanda estimada de coagulante DOM puede "
"forzarse a volver al rango razonable. Para evitar un dosis de coagulante "
"excesivamente bajo, la demanda de coagulante DOM puede limitarse a valores "
"positivos. Si se sabe que la demanda de coagulante DOM siempre supera un "
"valor mayor, ese valor mayor puede usarse como límite inferior. El límite "
"superior puede establecerse basándose en la observación de la calidad del "
"agua bruta."

#: ../../Operation/Coagulant_Automation.rst:123
